 "issue_title": "**Wrong-sign dn/dT** `material_database.py:330-334`",
 "issue_body": "Schott TIE-19 requires `\u0394n=(n\u00b2\u22121)/2n\u00b7[D\u0394T+\u2026+(E\u0394T+\u2026)/(\u03bb\u00b2\u2212\u03bbTK\u00b2)]`.\n   Code leaves D unscaled and drops `1/(\u03bb\u00b2\u2212\u03bbTK\u00b2)`.\n   BK7 \u0394T=+10K gives \u22129.7e-6 vs correct \u2248+1.7e-6 \u2014 wrong sign.\n   Poisons all `environmental.py:108` defocus.",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/pmaasz/openLens/issues/250",
 "pr": 268,
 "pr_title": "fix(materials): use Schott TIE-19 thermal model with catalog constants",
 "pr_body": "Replace the ad-hoc temperature correction (unscaled D terms plus a dispersion-free E term, yielding the wrong sign for BK7: -9.7e-6 for +10 K) with the exact TIE-19 absolute-index model\r\ndn=(n^2-1)/2n*[D0*dT+D1*dT^2+D2*dT^3+(E0*dT+E1*dT^2)/(wl^2-tk^2)], T0=20 C, wavelength in um. Add the lambda_tk_um field.\r\n\r\nReplace the incorrect built-in D/E values with verified Schott catalog data (N-BK7, SF11, F2, Lithosil-Q fused silica; refractiveindex.info / Schott Zemax catalog). BK7 now gives +1.45e-6/K at the d-line with blue > red thermal dispersion. Strengthen temperature tests with absolute-shift bounds.",
 "fix_commit": "17c781370abf3cfb88c9fc0ef28ac05a84f41175",
